        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man's robe('choga') of red woollen fabric embroidered with gold- and silver-wrapped thread and lined with silk.  This robe is decorated with typical northern-Indian and Kashmiri motifs, such as the single flower in staggered rows and the 'buti'(mango, cone or paisley pattern) in the borders and corners.  In Lahore, a variety of the Kashmiri style of chain-stitch embroidery was used in both silk and gold threads to embellish woollen robes and caps."@en ;
